### `reviewText(r)` Places-v1 unwrap (v0.60.156 — PR #397)

Local helper defined at outer scope in `index.js` (above `handleMichelinSearch` + `extractDishes` so the cuisine-chip path can re-use it). Signature:

```js
function reviewText(r) {
  if (!r) return '';
  const t = r.text;
  if (!t) return '';
  if (typeof t === 'string') return t;
  if (typeof t === 'object' && typeof t.text === 'string') return t.text;
  return '';
}
```

Handles both:
- **Places v1 shape** — `{ text: { text: '…', languageCode: 'en' } }` (current, since the Places API migration earlier in 2026).
- **Legacy bare-string shape** — `{ text: '…' }` (defensive — no-op for any source still returning the old form).

Called at 5 sites:

| Site | File | Line (approx) | Was | Now |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Michelin handler regex pool | `index.js` | ~6125 | `recent.map((r) => r.text \|\| '').join(' . ')` | `recent.map(reviewText).join(' . ')` |
| Michelin `v.recentReview` write | `index.js` | ~6140 | `String(recent[0].text \|\| '').slice(0, 200).trim()` | `reviewText(recent[0]).slice(0, 200).trim()` |
| `extractDishes` recent filter | `index.js` | ~9498 | `recent = v.reviews.filter((r) => r?.text)` | `recent = v.reviews.filter((r) => reviewText(r))` |
| `extractDishes` allText.map | `index.js` | ~9540 | `allText.map((t) => …)` (used to take raw `r.text`) | `allText` now built from `reviewText(r)` values |
| `extractDishes` return-`snippet` | `index.js` | ~9595 | `String(recent[0].text).slice(0, 200).trim()` | `reviewText(recent[0]).slice(0, 200).trim()` |
| `v.recentReview` fallback (cuisine-chip path) | `index.js` | ~9612 | `v.recentReview = String(v.reviews[0].text)…` | `v.recentReview = reviewText(v.reviews[0])…` |

Without this unwrap, `String({ text: '…', languageCode: 'en' })` coerces to the literal string `"[object Object]"` — a valid string, so every `typeof === 'string'` guard downstream passed it through unchanged. The v0.60.154 + v0.60.155 belt-and-braces guards stay in place but are now redundant on the happy path.

### Client-side page history machinery in `App.jsx` (v0.60.154 — PR #395)

Stateful additions:

```js
const [pages, setPages] = useState([]);
const [cursor, setCursor] = useState(0);

useEffect(() => {
  const p = pages[cursor];
  if (!p) return;
  setVenues(p.venues || []);
  setComboInfo(p.comboInfo || null);
  setMisrepNote(p.misrepNote || null);
  setCookMethodPivot(p.cookMethodPivot || null);
  setSessionFull(!!p.sessionFull);
  setPageStackDepth(Number.isFinite(p.pageStackDepth) ? p.pageStackDepth : 0);
  setMichelinRemaining(p.michelinRemaining || null);
  setExhaustedNote(!!p.exhausted);
  setPoolCount(Number.isFinite(p.poolCount) ? p.poolCount : 0);
  if (p.criteriaState && typeof p.criteriaState === 'object') setState(p.criteriaState);
  if (typeof p.freeText === 'string') setNlText(p.freeText);
  if (p.locationAnchor !== undefined) setLocationAnchor(p.locationAnchor || null);
  if (p.searchCenter !== undefined) setSearchCenter(p.searchCenter || null);
}, [cursor]);  // intentionally only on cursor change
```

Page payload (`runSearch` push at line ~610):

```js
const newPage = {
  venues, comboInfo, misrepNote, cookMethodPivot,
  sessionFull, pageStackDepth, michelinRemaining,
  exhausted, poolCount,
  criteriaSnap: stateSig(snap),
  criteriaState: JSON.parse(JSON.stringify(snap)),  // deep clone
  freeText: nlText,
  locationAnchor: { ...locationAnchor },
  searchCenter: { lat, lng },
  isMichelin
};
```

Caps: `isMichelin ? 11 : 17`. Push logic truncates the forward branch (`prev.slice(0, cursor + 1)`) then appends, then overflows oldest-first (`next.length > cap ? next.slice(next.length - cap) : next`). Cursor advances to the tail except on the very first push (`pages.length === 0 && prev === 0`) where it stays at 0.

Per Codex review on PR #395: the **criteriaState + freeText + locationAnchor + searchCenter** persistence was added so back-walks restore not just the venue list but also the chips / loading-hint trigger / copy-all heading / next 🔍 round-trip target. Prior to this fix the back-walked page showed the right venues but the rest of the UI described whatever the user had typed *after* navigating away.

### Per-criteria seen-set reset on TMA mount (v0.60.155 — PR #396)

`startSession` in `cuisine-session.js` now also DELetes every `cuisine:seen:<chatId>:*` SET key for the calling chatId (via `SCAN MATCH` + pipelined `DEL`). The per-criteria seen-set is the long-lived `cuisine:seen:<chatId>:<criteriaHash>` SET (no TTL — only cleared on explicit ↺ Start over). Wiping it on every TMA mount means a multi-week session no longer drifts into "every criteria returns zero new venues". The mount-side call (`POST /api/cuisine/session/start` fired by the TMA on `App.jsx` mount) was already there from v0.60.146 — the reset is now an additional inner step inside that handler.

The explicit ↺ Start over button still works as before (per-criteria reset only); this new path resets ALL per-criteria seen-sets at on

