- **[INTENT]** Operator security-hardening turn. Three priorities listed: (1) Telegram-WebApp `initData` auth gate, (2) API-key budget caps, (3) per-chatId rate limiting. Operator chose #1.

- **[DELTA]**

  **`twa-auth.js`** —

  *Added* `requireInitDataFromBodyOrHeader(req, res, next)`:
  ```js
  function requireInitDataFromBodyOrHeader(req, res, next) {
    if (process.env.SKIP_INIT_DATA_AUTH === 'true') {
      req.tg = { user: null, devBypass: true };
      return next();
    }
    const initData = req.headers['x-telegram-init-data'] || req.body?.initData || '';
    const verified = verifyInitData(initData, process.env.TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN);
    if (!verified) {
      const ip = req.headers['x-forwarded-for'] || req.socket?.remoteAddress || 'unknown';
      const ua = (req.headers['user-agent'] || 'unknown').slice(0, 80);
      console.warn(`[twa-auth] 401 ${req.method} ${req.path} ip=${ip} ua="${ua}"`);
      return res.status(401).json({ error: 'invalid initData' });
    }
    req.tg = verified;
    return next();
  }

  module.exports = { verifyInitData, requireInitData, requireInitDataFromBodyOrHeader };
  ```

  *Hardened* the existing `verifyInitData` hash compare:
  ```js
  // Before:
  if (computedHash !== hash) return null;

  // After (constant-time):
  let hashOk = false;
  try {
    hashOk = crypto.timingSafeEqual(Buffer.from(computedHash, 'hex'), Buffer.from(hash, 'hex'));
  } catch { hashOk = false; }
  if (!hashOk) return null;
  ```

  Net: ~30 LOC added to `twa-auth.js`.

  **`index.js`** — single import + single `app.use`:
  ```js
  const { requireInitData, verifyInitData, requireInitDataFromBodyOrHeader } = require('./twa-auth');
  …
  app.use('/api/cuisine', requireInitDataFromBodyOrHeader);

  app.get('/api/cuisine/catalogue', (_req, res) => { … });
  ```
  Placed directly before the first `/api/cuisine/*` route (line ~7838). All 17 routes + the two GETs inherit the gate. The 19 inline `verifyInitData(req.body?.initData, …)` calls remain — defense in depth, no risk of regression.

  **`__tests__/twa-auth.test.js`** — 17 new tests (8 `verifyInitData` + 2 `requireInitData` + 7 `requireInitDataFromBodyOrHeader`). Covers happy/tampered/expired/missing-hash/null-inputs/malformed-user paths, header-vs-body precedence, dev bypass enable + strict-string check.

  **`package.json`** — `0.60.166 → 0.60.167` (PATCH).

  **`doc/Journal/journal-0_60_167-14_05_26-2055.md`** — this entry (#133).

  **`doc/.serial-state.yml`** — `journal 132 → 133`, `commit 139 → 140`; re-anchored to `14-05 '26 20:55 SGT`.

- **[VERIFICATION (sandbox)]**

  ```bash
  $ node --check index.js && node --check twa-auth.js
  syntax OK
  $ npm test -- --run
   Test Files  57 passed (57)
        Tests  1757 passed (1757)        # +17 tests from twa-auth.test.js
  $ (cd web/cuisine && npm run build)
   ✓ built in 2.20s                       # client unchanged — sanity only
  ```

- **[STATUS]** STAGED → PROD on next Railway deploy after squash-merge. **No client change required** — the v2 TMA's `postJson` already body-stuffs initData; existing v1 endpoints already pass it via header. Both modes accepted.

- **[TEST]** Post-deploy verification:

  **Positive (normal use)**:
  - Open Cuisine TMA → cuisine search / warm-start / copy-all → all succeed identically to v0.60.166. Railway tail shows zero `[twa-auth] 401` lines for the operator's chatId.
  - Inline `verifyInitData(req.body?.initData, …)` calls still see the same body payload — no change in handler behaviour.

  **Negative (attacker probes — synthetic)**:
  - `curl -X POST https://soleat-prod.up.railway.app/api/cuisine/warm-start -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'` → expect HTTP 401 + `[twa-auth] 401 POST /api/cuisine/warm-start ip=… ua="curl/…"` in Railway tail.
  - `curl https://soleat-prod.up.railway.app/api/cuisine/catalogue` → expect HTTP 401 (was: HTTP 200 with the cuisine catalogue JSON).
  - Replay a stale initData (auth_date > 24h old) → 401.
  - Tamper one byte of the hash → 401.

  **Dev bypass**:
  - Railway preview deploys (or local `SKIP_INIT_DATA_AUTH=true node index.js`) → curl succeeds, `req.tg.devBypass === true`. Prod env never sets this.

- **[KNOWN GAPS]**

  - **DF-53 NEW** — same chokepoint pattern owed for `/api/menu/*`, `/api/hawker/*`, `/api/transport/*`, `/api/oversight/*` (the other four TMAs). Same middleware, same `app.use` line. Likely a half-hour follow-up — left as a separate PR so the cuisine-only blast radius of this change is reviewable on its own.
  - **DF-54 NEW** — per-chatId Redis sliding-window rate limit on the hot endpoints (`/api/cuisine/search`, `/api/cuisine/copy-all`, `/api/cuisine/place-autocomplete`, `/api/cuisine/nl-query`). Stops a compromised account from being weaponised against Google Places / Gemini quota even after passing the auth gate. The operator listed this as security priority #3.
  - **DF-55 NEW** — API-key budget caps in Google Cloud Console / Gemini / Anthropic consoles (zero-code, operator-side dashboard work). Security priority #2.
  - **DF-56 NEW** — simplify the 19 inline `verifyInitData(req.body?.initData, …)` calls to read `req.tg.user.id` (set by the new middleware) instead of re-running verify. Pure cleanup, zero behavioural change, ~40 LOC removed. Defer to a quiet pass.
  - **DF-49 / DF-50 / DF-51 / DF-52 (carried)** — petFriendly strict/fallback fixture test; conditional fieldmask; LocationField no-auto-fire integration test; filter-key wiring lint.
  - **DF-47 / DF-48 (carried)** — `insideSG` + `/\bjohor\b/i` unit tests; radius-slider-reset-on-pick.
  - **DF-44 / DF-45 / DF-46 / DF-40 / DF-41 / DF-42 / DF-43** — carried from prior PRs.

